### PHASE 1 - is the decomposition real?
dev: 200 triples

Each component is run alone. First its accuracy on the whole split,
then split by whether annotators marked the matching aspect: a real
component scores higher where it was marked.

=== component 'theme'  vs aspect 'abstract_theme' ===
    overall                      55.00% [48.08, 61.74]   n=200   AT CHANCE
    cannot test strata: 190 and 0

=== component 'action'  vs aspect 'course_of_actions' ===
    overall                      54.50% [47.58, 61.25]   n=200   AT CHANCE
    where annotators marked it   61.36% [50.92, 70.86]   n=88
    where they did not           52.63% [31.71, 72.67]   n=19
    difference +8.7 pts   z=+0.70  p=0.481   as predicted

=== component 'outcome'  vs aspect 'outcomes' ===
    overall                      54.00% [47.08, 60.77]   n=200   AT CHANCE
    where annotators marked it   52.50% [37.50, 67.06]   n=40
    where they did not           57.75% [46.15, 68.55]   n=71
    difference -5.2 pts   z=-0.53  p=0.593   BACKWARDS

Read the direction before the p-value. These strata are small, so a
non-significant difference in the right direction is weak support, and
a difference in the wrong direction is a problem whatever its p-value.

